senses.gloss:
vaipulya, nt.
(1) (also vaitulya, q.v., and see below; doubtless secondarily modified by confusion with Skt. vaipulya from vipula), (work of) great extent, or acc. to Burnouf, Intr. 〔62 f.〕, development: as one of the 9 (Dharmas) or 12 (Mvy) types of works in the canon, Dharmas 〔62〕; Mvy 〔1276〕 (in this sense seems to correspond to Pali vedalla as one of the 9 aṅga of the canon, cf. vaidalya); ˚lya-sūtra, applied by SP and LV to their own texts and similar [] works, SP 〔1.3〕; 〔46.4〕; 〔98.3, 11〕; LV 〔7.9〕; see also mahā-vai˚, and refs. s.v. vaitulya;
(2) n. of a mountain: var. for Vaidalya (2), Dbh 〔96.2〕 (one of the ten great mountains of the earth; in Pali Vepulla is one of the mountains surrounding Rājagaha).
